  "uprn": "100023407937",
  "decision_date": "09/01/2007",
  "description": "DEMOLITION OF EXISTING BUILDINGS AND ERECTION OF A PART FIVE STOREY / PART SIX STOREY BUILDING COMPRISING ONE RESTAURANT UNIT AND ONE A2 UNIT AT GROUND AND LOWER GROUND FLOOR WITH THIRTEEN FLATS OVER, INCORPORATING LANDSCAPING.",
  "site_name": "Former",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "02/12/2004",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "TW8 8JB",
  "street_name": "London Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major dwellings",
  "lapsed_date": "08/01/2010",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 4 - No development shall take place until full details of both hard and soft landscape works have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority and these works shall be carried out as approved.  These details shall include (proposed finished levels or contours; means of enclosure; car parking layouts; other vehicle and pedestrian access and circulation areas; hard surfacing material; proposed and existing functional services above and below ground (eg drainage power, communications cables, pipelines etc. indicating lines, manholes, supports etc);\r\n\r\nSoft landscape works shall include (planting plans; written specifications (including cultivation and other operations associated with plant and grass establishment); schedules of plants, noting species, plant sizes and proposed numbers/densities where appropriate; implementation programme).\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - . All hard and soft landscape works shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details. The works shall be carried out prior to occupation of any part of the development or in accordance with a programme agreed with the Local Planning Authority",
    "Condition : 6 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8:30am to 5:30pm on Mondays to Friday and 9am to 1pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 7 - Deliveries to any commercial premises once constructed shall only be made to or despatched from the site between the hours of 7:00am to 6:30pm.",
    "Condition : 8 - No fans, louvers, ducts or other external plant shall be installed  without the prior written approval of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 9 - 9. The access doorway to the ground level commercial units shall have a minimum clear width of 1800mm for double doors and 900mm for single width doors, a level surface or ramp between the pavement and the floor and a door handle of not more than 1m above ground level.",
    "Condition : 10 - The parking, loading and turning spaces shown on the approved plans shall be constructed and available for use before the first occupation of any part of the development and such spaces shall not be used for any other purposes.\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 11 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 12 - The commercial units shall not be amalgamated without the prior written consent of the Local Planning Authority and for no other purposes whatsoever.",
    "Condition : 13 - 13. The use shall not commence until a scheme for control of fumes and odours including details of sound attenuation for any necessary plant has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority in writing",
    "Condition : 14 - The scheme approved under condition 13 shall be fully implemented before the (A3 use, specified use, restaurant) opens to customers",
    "Condition : 15 - The A3/A2 uses hereby permitted shall not be open to customers outside the following times 10am to 11pm.",
    "Condition : 16 - A replacement flood defence wall shall be constructed to a minimum level of 6.4 metres AOD(N) with associated compensatory flood storage works, river wall replacement works and associated riverbank enhancement works in accordance with drawing numbers 34515/FS/02 and 34515/GA/02 shall be carried out prior to first occupation of the development.\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 17 - 17. Signs shall be placed on the internal face of the flood wall in prominent positions, to inform the owners/occupiers of the restaurant \tat ground level of the risk of flooding. Details of the wording and design of these signs shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority prior to development commencing",
    "Condition : 18 - Details of the landscaped area adjacent to the river (and any other \t\r\nplanting within 8metre of the top of bank of the river), should be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority prior to development commencing. The area should comprise of locally native plant species only, of UK genetic provenance.  There should be no hardstanding or fencing within this area.\r\n",
    "Condition : 19 - The sheet piling should be faced with appropriate material for the entire length of the site, in order to improve both the ecology and the aesthetics of the bank.  Wood cladding of the sheet piling, back filling of piling gaps with gravel and construction of baton shelving would be an appropriate measure.  Shelving should be planted with appropriate locally native species of UK genetic stock. Details of these works must be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority prior to development commencing and all work should be completed before occupation of the new development",
    "Condition : 20 - There shall be no light spill into the watercourse or adjacent river corridor habitat.  To achieve this, and to comply with sustainability, artificial lighting should be directional and focused with cowlings to light sources in close proximity to the river corridor",
    "Condition : 21 - The proposed development will provide a building similar in form and design to that currently on site improving the appearance of the gateway into Brentford. The overall scheme is considered to preserve and enhance the adjoining conservation area, makes best use of previously developed land in a suitable location and will not detract from the appearance of the remaining part of the original terrace which is of townscape character. The small scale, commercial uses restore the historical use of this terrace, helping to identify the entrance to Brentford Town Centre. This is in accordance with polices IMP.1.1 Integrating land use & provision of transport, IMP.3.1 Brentford Regeneration Area, IMP.5.1 High Quality Building and Urban Design, and S.3.1 (New Retail Development) of the adopted London Borough of Hounslow Unitary Plan 2003."
